From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:41:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/93] drm/apple: send a paired mode set's calls in the
 engine's firmware 27 build

The paired mode set (a mode too wide for one engine, run on two) sends its IOMFB calls through dcp_peer_video_call_stream() (and the opt-in peer setup diagnostic through peer_setup_test_store()), naming them by their 27.0 IDs. Firmware 27.2 renumbered the IOMobileFramebufferAP methods, and an ID the firmware does not know panics it: on a 27.2 stub the paired prepare's set_display_device went out as A411 and crashed both engines.

Record every paired-mode and sleep method ID in each firmware 27 build's table (the shifted IDs on 27.2, plus the unchanged paired/DSC hand-off and sleep calls) while keeping them optional for single-engine boot admission in iomfb_v27_missing_method(). Translate each call's ID through iomfb_v27_tag(): on 27.0 (including the J714s copy) every ID is sent unchanged; on a renumbered build every ID must come from the build's table, returning -EOPNOTSUPP instead of sending an unmapped ID. Update the t6041-v27-admission host test fixture for the table helpers it extracts.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
